{
  "resolutions": [
    {
      "issue_id": "584d57e8677a411ea955c703704d6fe0",
      "target_version": 1,
      "original_question": "The direction from G_apply to O_commit is plausible: the documentation describes commitment notification preceding leader FSM dispatch, and commitment.go exposes the notification and index getter. However, the actual leader consumer is absent. The supplied appendEntries implementation shows a follower consuming LeaderCommitIndex, which does not establish the leader handoff. Confirming this dependency requires locating the leader's commit-channel handling and tracing the selected index into processLogs and FSM dispatch.",
      "source_ids": [
        "commitment.go:1:104",
        "raft.go:450:850",
        "raft.go:1200:1439",
        "docs/apply.md:101:116",
        "fsm.go:1:180"
      ],
      "rationale": "The newly supplied leaderLoop receives commitment notifications, reads commitment.getCommitIndex(), selects inflight entries whose indexes do not exceed that index, and passes the last selected index and index-keyed futures to processLogs. processLogs prepares entries through that limit and sends command commitTuples to fsmMutateCh. prepareLog explicitly includes LogCommand. The supplied runFSM closure applies commands and completes their associated futures. This establishes the particular leader-to-FSM dependency that the stored issue could not previously verify. It does not establish every completion path or the truth of reported replication progress.",
      "residual_issue_ids": [
        "e8b251f5fc044734a4acdf606a072c08",
        "0dd8ad9cd1064dd2838b32bac188210c",
        "09ea4aa00f384f4d84f3ebd5a1bf0207"
      ],
      "scope_limitations": [
        "This resolution establishes the leader handoff supporting R_apply_commit, not end-to-end Apply correctness.",
        "Report durability, configuration-history safety, notification delivery and the complete FSM receive loop remain outside this handoff judgment."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "resolves_issue_ids": [
    "584d57e8677a411ea955c703704d6fe0"
  ],
  "supersedes_task_ids": [],
  "resolution_rationale": "Only the missing leader-consumer issue is resolved: the added raft.go ranges expose its actual index selection and FSM queue handoff. The proposed F2 updates the relation's stale grounding and corrects U_commit's broader-than-obligation monotonicity question. The unit issue remains open until the revised unit is accepted and reviewed. Other stored issues are not cleared by this invocation.",
  "items": [
    {
      "scope_limitations": [
        "The goal excludes unsuccessful-Apply no-effect guarantees and user-initiated snapshot replacement."
      ],
      "target_id": "G_apply",
      "aspect": "applicability",
      "status": "needs_reading",
      "source_ids": [
        "docs/apply.md:1:100",
        "docs/apply.md:101:116",
        "api.go:803:907",
        "fsm.go:1:180",
        "commitment.go:1:104",
        "raft.go:450:850",
        "raft.go:1200:1439"
      ],
      "explanation": "The goal has an explicit expectation: docs/apply.md describes durable quorum storage before application, and FSM.Apply requires majority commitment. The API permits uncertainty after ErrLeadershipLost, which does not contradict the goal's restriction to successful reports. The added leader code establishes a concrete commitment-to-command-dispatch dependency. However, the supplied packet does not establish what persistence and membership contracts make 'durable' and 'applicable cluster configuration' precise for the current fault and configuration scope. Retain the goal as a supported candidate while reading the storage interface and membership contract.",
      "alternatives": "Snapshot catch-up can supply prefix support without retransmitting each original log. A storage implementation may also have persistence semantics that require an explicit configuration or fault qualification; the documentation's durable-storage statement must not simply be weakened to match such behavior.",
      "counterexample_reasoning": "Correct numeric commitment can coexist with reports unsupported by durable storage or with an unsafe configuration history. Thus all selected local obligations could hold while the goal's bad outcome still occurs. These are dependency gaps, not observed executions.",
      "limitations": [
        "The selected storage backend and its crash or partial-failure contract are not supplied.",
        "Membership eligibility and historical quorum support are not established by observing the current voter map.",
        "Issue e8b251f5fc044734a4acdf606a072c08 remains open."
      ]
    },
    {
      "scope_limitations": [
        "This obligation concerns reported numbers within one commitment instance; it excludes report truth, configuration legality, threshold initialization correctness and end-to-end completion."
      ],
      "target_id": "O_commit",
      "aspect": "applicability",
      "status": "no_issue_found",
      "source_ids": [
        "commitment.go:1:104",
        "docs/apply.md:1:100",
        "raft.go:450:850",
        "raft.go:1200:1439"
      ],
      "explanation": "The component comments assign monotonically increasing commitment from voter progress and require reaching the first index of the leader's term. These attributed responsibilities support the local obligation independently of its sorting implementation. The new caller material also shows one commitment object initialized during leader setup and consumed by leaderLoop. Provisionally, the obligation applies to this component scope.",
      "alternatives": "Previously established commitIndex may remain unchanged after voter replacement without acquiring fresh support from the replacement map. Stored progress need only be nondecreasing when updated by match, not across removal and later reintroduction.",
      "counterexample_reasoning": "A same-instance match call that lowered stored progress, or an advancement lacking current-map majority support, would contradict the selected responsibility. A reset caused by removing and later reintroducing a voter would not violate the match-report clause.",
      "limitations": [
        "This is a source-based interpretation, not an executed check.",
        "The positive interpretation repeats the substance of issue 816ba277d65a4acb950f4454cfe49ab9; no separate resolution is claimed for that stored issue."
      ]
    },
    {
      "scope_limitations": [
        "The decomposition covers component transitions rather than global consensus history."
      ],
      "target_id": "O_commit",
      "aspect": "decomposition",
      "status": "no_issue_found",
      "source_ids": [
        "commitment.go:1:104",
        "docs/apply.md:1:100"
      ],
      "explanation": "Initialization establishes tracked voters and startIndex; match admits only increasing reports for tracked voters; setConfiguration replaces the voter map while preserving surviving entries; recalculate chooses the strict-majority threshold and guards advancement. These responsibilities cover the selected local transitions. Majority support belongs to the map at an advancement, whereas historical commitIndex remains monotonic across map replacement.",
      "alternatives": "Removed voter progress can be forgotten and later initialized to zero. Retaining commitment previously achieved under another configuration is distinct from requiring every current state to support a fresh advancement.",
      "counterexample_reasoning": "For n tracked voters, the ascending element at floor((n-1)/2) has at least floor(n/2)+1 entries at or above it, including even voter counts. This explains the arithmetic association without proving the implementation by execution. Even perfect arithmetic leaves dishonest or stale reports, incorrect startIndex and unsafe configuration histories unresolved.",
      "limitations": [
        "No model or executable correspondence check is supplied.",
        "The interpretation of report monotonicity remains confined to match operations.",
        "Issue fe2c5595549a4f378a3b8fa512c910b8 is not separately resolved by this repeated interpretation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "scope_limitations": [
        "The binding covers initialization, not caller correctness."
      ],
      "target_id": "B_newCommitment",
      "aspect": "decomposition",
      "status": "no_issue_found",
      "source_ids": [
        "commitment.go:1:104",
        "docs/apply.md:1:100",
        "raft.go:450:850"
      ],
      "explanation": "The newCommitment declaration at line 35 and behavior range 35–48 match the supplied source. The function creates zero-valued progress only for Voter entries and stores the supplied startIndex. Its authoritative association to O_commit and direct unit use accurately identify establishment of the examined state. setupLeaderState now supplies an observed caller using the latest configuration and getLastIndex()+1.",
      "alternatives": "A caller could establish the same threshold through another validated initialization mechanism; this binding establishes only the actual constructor's behavior.",
      "counterexample_reasoning": "An incorrect caller-supplied threshold could undermine Apply while constructor behavior and local arithmetic remain satisfied. The binding does not purport to exclude that outcome.",
      "limitations": [
        "Observing getLastIndex()+1 does not establish recovery correctness, index exhaustion behavior or configuration validity."
      ]
    },
    {
      "scope_limitations": [
        "The binding covers numeric report admission, not durable-prefix production."
      ],
      "target_id": "B_match",
      "aspect": "decomposition",
      "status": "no_issue_found",
      "source_ids": [
        "commitment.go:1:104",
        "docs/apply.md:1:100",
        "raft.go:1200:1439"
      ],
      "explanation": "The match declaration at line 77 and range 77–84 match the source. Membership filtering and the strict-increase guard directly implement the report-update clause of O_commit. The association and direct code use do not import the stronger disk-agreement guarantee from the comment. The new dispatchLogs material exposes a local producer calling match only after StoreLogs returns successfully.",
      "alternatives": "Local writes, ordinary replication and snapshot catch-up can produce reports through different mechanisms; equivalent numeric input does not establish equivalent persistence.",
      "counterexample_reasoning": "A numerically increasing report about an incorrect or non-durable prefix passes this filter. That possibility supports the explicit producer boundary rather than invalidating this binding.",
      "limitations": [
        "StoreLogs success semantics and follower response correlation remain unverified."
      ]
    },
    {
      "scope_limitations": [
        "The binding covers voter-map replacement, not legal membership histories."
      ],
      "target_id": "B_setConfiguration",
      "aspect": "decomposition",
      "status": "no_issue_found",
      "source_ids": [
        "commitment.go:1:104",
        "docs/apply.md:1:100",
        "raft.go:450:850",
        "raft.go:1200:1439"
      ],
      "explanation": "The declaration at line 53 and behavior range 53–64 correctly identify setConfiguration. It rebuilds the voter map under lock, copies surviving IDs' progress, initializes absent IDs to zero and recalculates. The O_commit association and direct use are accurate. appendConfigurationEntry supplies an actual setter call, while configurationChangeChIfStable exposes relevant caller conditions; the complete transition eligibility path is still unestablished.",
      "alternatives": "The component could retain removed-ID history, but the supplied implementation does not. No applicable expectation requires such retention.",
      "counterexample_reasoning": "Removing and later reintroducing an ID can lower its newly stored value relative to its former value. This contradicts U_commit's unqualified wording, not the binding description or O_commit's match-call monotonicity clause.",
      "limitations": [
        "nextConfiguration and the complete configuration-change admission path have not been inspected."
      ]
    },
    {
      "scope_limitations": [
        "The binding covers advancement arithmetic and its notification call, not delivery or consumption guarantees."
      ],
      "target_id": "B_recalculate",
      "aspect": "decomposition",
      "status": "no_issue_found",
      "source_ids": [
        "commitment.go:1:104",
        "docs/apply.md:1:100",
        "raft.go:450:850"
      ],
      "explanation": "The recalculate declaration at line 88 and range 88–104 match the supplied source. The empty-map return, sorted majority selection, strictly increasing commitIndex guard and startIndex threshold correspond directly to O_commit. The association and unit's direct use identify the actual producer of examined advances.",
      "alternatives": "Equivalent quorum calculations could avoid sorting. This source mapping does not make sorting itself the normative requirement.",
      "counterexample_reasoning": "An unchanged commitIndex can exceed current-map support after configuration replacement without violating an advancement-only obligation. A checker requiring current support in every state would therefore exceed the intended responsibility.",
      "limitations": [
        "asyncNotifyCh delivery semantics are not supplied.",
        "No predicate encoding or executed arithmetic check is present."
      ]
    },
    {
      "scope_limitations": [
        "The relation expresses one necessary ordinary-leader-path dependency, not sufficiency for G_apply."
