        "replication.go:202:298",
        "raft.go:1200:1439",
        "raft.go:1440:1584",
        "transport.go:1:74"
      ],
      "explanation": "The boundary correctly points from numeric consumption toward prefix-support production. match's comment requires agreement on disk through the reported index, but its body verifies only voter identity membership and increasing numbers. dispatchLogs now exposes the local StoreLogs-to-match handoff. replicateTo exposes successful-response consumption through the unresolved updateLastAppended callee, and appendEntries stores new entries before success. These facts justify retaining the boundary without treating its producer guarantee as established.",
      "alternatives": "Ordinary AppendEntries, pipelined completion and snapshot installation may each establish prefix support. Their identity and persistence guarantees require their own investigation.",
      "counterexample_reasoning": "All numeric O_commit clauses can hold while a report misidentifies a prefix or storage success lacks the required persistence. The explicit truncation-then-StoreLogs-failure comment in appendEntries remains contrary evidence requiring investigation; its consequences are not established here.",
      "limitations": [
        "updateLastAppended, pipeline and snapshot progress producers remain unread.",
        "Transport response correlation and storage failure semantics remain unresolved.",
        "Issue 0dd8ad9cd1064dd2838b32bac188210c remains open; accepting the boundary direction does not resolve its producer guarantees."
      ]
    },
    {
      "scope_limitations": [
        "Network, crash durability, election safety, configuration-transition safety and end-to-end Apply remain excluded.",
        "goal_observable=false correctly prevents a local result from establishing G_apply."
