        "docs/apply.md:1:100",
        "raft.go:450:850",
        "raft.go:1200:1439"
      ],
      "explanation": "The four direct code uses coherently cover O_commit. However, the main audit question and ordered coverage point ask for unqualified monotonic stored progress across map replacement. setConfiguration preserves only surviving IDs and forgets removed IDs, so this question is stronger than O_commit's match-report clause. The proposed F2 changes only these two strings inside audit_question, distinguishing monotonic commitIndex and increasing match updates from removal and readdition resets.",
      "alternatives": "A permanent per-ServerID history requirement would need a separate attributed expectation and a different obligation. No such requirement is established by the supplied materials.",
      "counterexample_reasoning": "As a source-derived illustration, match(A, 5), removal of A, and later reintroduction of A can produce a newly tracked value of zero. This is not an executed counterexample or an established legal membership history. It demonstrates why the current question could classify permitted component replacement behavior as a violation.",
      "limitations": [
        "Issue 09ea4aa00f384f4d84f3ebd5a1bf0207 remains open until the proposed revision is accepted and reviewed.",
        "Ordered coverage must retain commitment-instance identity and ServerID correlation; no sequence reachability has been executed.",
        "Arbitrary setter sequences do not establish legal cluster executions."
      ]
    }
